  "architecture_notes": [
    "Operational state changes and finance outbox writes must share one DB transaction.",
    "Delivery is at-least-once and relies on downstream idempotency.",
    "Workers use short-lived delivery leases to avoid concurrent processing.",
    "Retries are bounded with exponential backoff and dead-letter quarantine.",
    "External provider side effects must never be replayed by this accounting delivery layer.",
    "The next implementation phase should wire existing operational modules into the outbox."
